@startuml flow-2-track-book
' Part 2 — Track THIS request's Task, then book when it has been acted on
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Calibri
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #001D34
  LifeLineBorderColor #757579
  ParticipantBorderColor #00A9CE
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E6F6FA
  ParticipantFontColor #001D34
  ActorBorderColor #00A9CE
  ActorBackgroundColor #E6F6FA
}

actor "Referrer\n(Placer)" as R
participant "Referral\nServer" as S
participant "Imaging Provider\n(Filler)" as F

note over R, S
  Track **this referral's Task** — Task?focus=ServiceRequest/{id} —
  to know whether **this specific request** has been acted on,
  not generic Slot availability. The filler publishes availability
  independently.
end note

R -> S : GET Task?focus=ServiceRequest/{id} (poll or subscribe)

alt Task accepted / scheduled — request acted on
  S --> R : Task (accepted) + linked Slots
  R -> S : search Slot / POST Appointment (proposed, basedOn ServiceRequest)
  F -> S : confirm: Appointment booked, Slot busy, Task in-progress
else Task still requested / on-hold — not yet acted on
  S --> R : Task (requested / on-hold, statusReason)
  note right of R : keep watching the Task; retry once accepted
end

@enduml
